<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns#"
                  xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/processes/ns#"
                  id="Definitions_Process_GraphDetanglement" targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns#" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="administrator" name="Administrator"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="authoring-agent" name="Authoring agent"/>
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_Process_GraphDetanglement">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Process_GraphDetanglement" name="A sub-graph wants to leave" processRef="Process_GraphDetanglement"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_GraphDetanglement" name="A sub-graph wants to leave" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Part of a repository wants to leave, for size or a semantic reason: four gated stages measure it out of the graph before anything moves, and an administrator authorises the extraction. THE FOUR STAGES ARE GATES, NOT ADVICE, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE REASON THIS IS A DIAGRAM. `graph-detanglement.md` says "nothing moves until the stage before it measures zero" in prose, and prose is what an agent under pressure talks itself past. Each gate here is a DECISION TABLE: `workflow_complete` refuses a hand-supplied outcome at a `cat-harness.processes:decision` gateway, so the branch is computed from the counts a tool already produced rather than asserted.

THE SHARPEST GATE IS `Detangled?`, AND IT IS SHARP BECAUSE OF ITS RULE ORDER. `unassignedEdges &amp;gt; 0` returns `unknown` BEFORE the cross-edge rule is reached, so a zero cross-edge count over an unjudged corpus cannot be read as a pass. `repo-partition.ts` states it in its own voice — "these are not cross-edges, they are edges this tool declined to judge. Do not read them as clean" — and move 1 of the practice is exactly that sentence. A person can skip it. A table cannot.

EVERY GATE HAS A THIRD STATE AND NONE OF THEM RENDERS IT AS CLEAN. `Declared in place?` answers `unknown` on a declaration that did not parse rather than "not yet", because one says the work has not started and the other says nobody can tell. `Detangled?` answers `unknown` on an incomplete measurement. Both route to `End_Unknown`, which is a REFUSAL to advance — the process stops rather than proceeding on a guess.

DECLARING IS CHEAP AND EXTRACTING IS EXPENSIVE, WHICH IS THE POINT. Stage 1 moves nothing: the sub-graph is declared where it already sits, still inside the repository, still connected. The worked example was the WHO base harness's `methodologies/`, declared in place and lifted out whole when that harness became its own repository.

STAGE 2 IS A LOOP, AND THE LOOP IS LOAD-BEARING. `Prune, merge, factor, or reclassify` returns to `Measure` rather than to the gate, because an assignment is verified by RE-RUNNING and never by being locally reasonable — the obvious move, the one the tool's own message asks for, once took the count from 5 to 15. The four moves are the only four: the first three are the block-scale rule, and "the classification is wrong" is the fourth the repository scale adds because a module's layer is in doubt the way a block's chapter is not.

ISOLATION IS NOT ZERO EDGES. A sub-graph with no inbound edges can still carry no declaration, no namespace and no published artefact, and lifting that directory produces a repository that cannot say what it is. `bootstrap/` is the demonstrated case and the shape to match.

THE EXTRACTION IS A PERSON'S DECISION, AND THE LANE SAYS SO. `Authorise the extraction` sits in the Administrator lane because an extraction moves durable artefacts out of a repository, and `deletion-requires-confirmation` is not a courtesy the agent may waive: the agent reports what would move, and waits. The administrator lane is the one whose activities change the substrate every other diagram's lanes bind to, which is exactly what a repository cut does. DRAWN IN PHASES (owner, 2026-11-02, G5): each phase is its own diagram, called here, and the bean is opened and closed once at this level.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <cat-harness.processes:policy enforcement="strict"/>
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_Process_GraphDetanglement">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Agent" name="Authoring agent" partitionElementRef="authoring-agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>Runs every stage up to the edge of authorisation — brief, declare, measure, move-and-remeasure, isolate — and Task_Propose is the last thing it does off its own judgement: reporting sizes and what would break, then waiting. Verification here is always by RE-RUNNING the measurement rather than by an assignment being locally reasonable, which is why Task_Move loops back to Task_Measure and not to the gate — a move that looks right is not yet a move that measured right.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_Wants</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_BeanOpen</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_BeanYours</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_BeanNotYours</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Brief</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Detangle</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_MeasuredOut</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Extract</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Admin" name="Administrator" partitionElementRef="administrator">
        <bpmn:documentation>Reached only after Declared, Detangled and Isolated have each independently cleared — so this lane is never asked to judge the measurement, only whether an already-clean extraction may proceed. Declining is not a refusal back to unknown: End_Declined leaves the sub-graph declared, detangled and isolated in place, which is a real outcome of this process and not merely the absence of one.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Authorise</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Authorised</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_BeanClose</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_BeanClosedHow</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Extracted</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Declined</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Unknown</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_Wants" name="Size, or a semantic&#10;reason to separate">
      <bpmn:outgoing>F0</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_BeanOpen" name="Open the bean" calledElement="Process_BeanOpen">
      <bpmn:documentation>Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); the gateway after this reads which end it reached.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="bean-coordination"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F0</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_BeanYours" name="Bean claimed?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_BeanNotYours" name="Not yours —&#10;left alone">
      <bpmn:documentation>Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_3</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Brief" name="Brief the topic before&#10;touching anything">
      <bpmn:documentation>What am I doing and why is it worth doing; what do I already know, with each measurement's provenance; how do I plan to do it and WHAT WOULD FALSIFY THE APPROACH. A falsifier that never fires is decoration — this practice's own fired, took edges 5 to 12, and rewrote the plan.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="opening-brief"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Detangle" name="Declare, detangle&#10;and isolate it" calledElement="Process_KgSeparationDetangle">
      <bpmn:documentation>The four gates, stages 1-3: declared in place, detangled with the unassigned column first, and isolated. Each gate is a decision table with a third state, unknown.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="graph-detanglement"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_MeasuredOut" name="Measured out?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end the detangle phase reached: isolated, or could not determine.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F3</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Authorise" name="Authorise the&#10;extraction" calledElement="Process_KgSeparationAuthorise">
      <bpmn:documentation>Report what would move, then ask the administrator to authorise the extraction.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="deletion-requires-confirmation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Authorised" name="Authorised?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end the authorise phase reached.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F6</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Extract" name="Extract — a directory move,&#10;not a file-by-file sift">
      <bpmn:documentation>Only once edges are zero and the declaration stands alone: move the sub-graph out as one directory move, not a file-by-file sift. Its nested declaration resolves paths against its own directory, so moving the folder moves the graph. The five-point gate is in migration-plan.md Phase II.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="graph-detanglement"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_BeanClose" name="Close the bean" calledElement="Process_BeanClose">
      <bpmn:documentation>Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_BeanClosedHow" name="How did it end?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Which outcome the bean was closed with, so each ends at its own named end event. The bean is closed once, on every path (bpmn-authoring: open and close the bean at the top, once).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_5</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_6</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Extracted" name="Extracted">
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_5</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Declined" name="Stays where it is&#10;— declared, detangled, isolated">
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_6</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Unknown" name="UNKNOWN — stop.&#10;Not “not yet”, not clean">
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_7</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F0" sourceRef="Start_Wants" targetRef="Call_BeanOpen"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_2" sourceRef="Call_BeanOpen" targetRef="GW_BeanYours"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_1" name="claimed" sourceRef="GW_BeanYours" targetRef="Task_Brief"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_3" name="not yours" sourceRef="GW_BeanYours" targetRef="End_BeanNotYours"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F1" sourceRef="Task_Brief" targetRef="Call_Detangle"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F2" sourceRef="Call_Detangle" targetRef="GW_MeasuredOut"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F3" name="isolated" sourceRef="GW_MeasuredOut" targetRef="Call_Authorise"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F4" name="unknown" sourceRef="GW_MeasuredOut" targetRef="Call_BeanClose"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F5" sourceRef="Call_Authorise" targetRef="GW_Authorised"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F6" name="authorised" sourceRef="GW_Authorised" targetRef="Task_Extract"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F7" name="declined" sourceRef="GW_Authorised" targetRef="Call_BeanClose"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F8" sourceRef="Task_Extract" targetRef="Call_BeanClose"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_4" sourceRef="Call_BeanClose" targetRef="GW_BeanClosedHow"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_5" name="extracted" sourceRef="GW_BeanClosedHow" targetRef="End_Extracted"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_6" name="declined" sourceRef="GW_BeanClosedHow" targetRef="End_Declined"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_7" name="unknown" sourceRef="GW_BeanClosedHow" targetRef="End_Unknown"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_Process_GraphDetanglement">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_Process_GraphDetanglement" bpmnElement="Collaboration_Process_GraphDetanglement">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Participant_Process_GraphDetanglement" bpmnElement="Participant_Process_GraphDetanglement" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="130" y="60" width="2380" height="1250"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Agent" bpmnElement="Lane_Agent" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="60" width="2350" height="500"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Admin" bpmnElement="Lane_Admin" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="560" width="2350" height="750"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
